\frac{q_j(x_1-x_j)}{[(x_1\!-\!x_j)^2\!+\!(y_1\!-\!y_j)^2\!+\!(z_1\!-\!z_j)^2]^{3/2}},\notag

\end{align}

and so on.

Often it is convenient to ignore the fact that charges come in

packages like electrons and protons, and think of them as being spread

