\label{Eq:II:36:36}

\mathbf{B}_a=\mathbf{H}+\lambda\,\frac{\mathbf{M}}{\epsilon_0 c^2}.

\end{equation}

In the spherical hole approximation, we would have

$\lambda=\frac{1}{3}$, but, as you will see, we will want later to

use some other value, so we leave it as an adjustable parameter. Also,

we will take all the fields in the same direction so that we won’t

