(S_{xy})_{y=0}=\eta r\,\frac{d \omega}{d r}.

\end{equation}

(It is reasonable that $S$ should depend on $\partial \omega / \partial r$; when

there is no change in $\omega$ with $r$, the liquid is in uniform

